{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtIII","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardtiii"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Three fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(≈ 698.045 cents). Six fifths — A→E, B→F♯, F♯→C♯, C♯→A♭, E♭→B♭, B♭→F — are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma (≈ 700.000 cents). The remaining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"three fifths — E→B, A♭→E♭, F→C — are pure. The circle closes exactly:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"3×(1\/6) + 6×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"From ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Differs from ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtII","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only in the placement of the sixth-comma group on the flat side: E♭→B♭ is tempered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"here where it is pure in Neidhardt II, and F→C is pure here where it is tempered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in Neidhardt II.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"IvorTuning","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"title":"neidhardtIII","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE12neidhardtIIIAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Type Property","role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/neidhardtIII":{"abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtIII","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardtiii","kind":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"title":"neidhardtIII","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types."}],"title":"IvorTuning","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","abstract":[{"text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths.","type":"text"}],"title":"WellTemperament","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/neidhardtII":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt II (“Small City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtII","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"neidhardtII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text